hi there Steve Kaufman here today it's  the 30th of December 2019 it's near the  end of the year and we start a new  decade so it's a good time to sort of  take stock I think at the end of the  year is always the time people think  about you know what do I want to do next  year when Diet Eve this year personal  relationships personal development work  and so forth  so if we think of language learning is  so which is what I always talk about  here you know why do we learn languages  you know what is the purpose and I think  if we understand the purpose of language  learning I think that can influence how  we learn how we teach how we treat other  people who are learning or speaking  other languages if we understand what  the fundamental purpose of language  learning is and to me the fundamental  purpose of language learning is to enjoy  the language  I mean language gives us so much  enjoyment that's true even of our own  language through language we can  communicate with you know friends and  family we can enjoy books we can enjoy  movies we can enjoy the language itself  we can enjoy the things that we learned  through the language or that we hear  about through the language it's all  about enjoyment and so let me teach the  language and I always get back to  capital on this great Hungarian polyglot  she lived in the mostly in the 20th  century who had this formula so success  in language learning depends on our  attitude times the amount of time we  spend with the language divided by  inhibition and I add to that frustration  everything that's negative so attitude  obviously if we are teaching the  language the most important thing has to  be to create a positive attitude in the  learner so that the learner enjoys it  like in school  for example and somehow to get the  learner to spend time with the language  and to reduce everything that causes  inhibition frustration negative feelings  so then the question is why have tests  what's the purpose of tests in school  because I know many people countless  people English speakers in Canada who go  through the school system learning  French every day passing their tests and  never ever used the language never use  French not interested in French don't  read in French don't want fresh movies  other than with subtitles don't get into  everything all the enjoyment of the  language can bring you so why do we  teach in this way the number if I were  teaching school number one goal is how  do I get the learner to enjoy this  language or any language how do I get  the learner to get into the enjoyment of  language that has to be the number one  goal and if we assess our own activity  in language learning am i enjoying it am  i enjoying the language and enjoyment  can come in many different ways like  I've been learning Persian I speak it  extremely poorly and as a result I am  NOT interested in things Persian so I  read a book in English about a girl  growing up in Iran is called Arya and  there's various reviews suggest that  there's a lot of inaccuracies but it's  still it's an involvement with your  honor like came to me because I'm  learning Persian languages bring us  enjoyment that enjoyment to me is more  important than whether I nail the  grammar correctly so if enjoyment is and  it's very important to this that because  I spend a lot of time learning languages  going a bit crazy right now with my  Persian Arabic and Turkish but it's very  important that I am convinced and that's  true for any member that what I am doing  is worthwhile that the time that I spend  is time well spent this is good this is  bringing the enjoyment it'll bring me  probably some you know improvement in I  agree  but it's it's worth doing it's it's it's  bringing me rewarding things so it's  important that the in order to get  people to spend the time remember  catalogs formula altitude time /  inhibition we have to spend the time so  we have to feel at that time is well  spent  worthwhile enjoyable so similarly when  we comment on others who speak a  language and here I you know I had a  video there where I said that you get  negative comments I get negative  comments and Christine who put up this  wonderful video where she speaks many  languages get some negative comments and  why well some people commented well you  know she speaks so many languages and  Matt says that it takes three to five  years to become good in a language what  does that mean what is good in a  language mean you know if I can  understand if I can communicate with  errors I'm good okay I may not be a  native I may not even be near a native  but if I can understand what people are  saying and they can understand me I'm  good or good enough and it's not for us  to comment on other people's ability  that is meaningless we learned languages  for ourselves because we think it's  enjoyable to learn languages and when we  start Christine's video it's obvious  that she enjoys those languages and some  people commented well you know she  obviously stopped between each language  and you know she didn't get into great  depth and so maybe she doesn't know them  like thank you these people know nothing  about her level of skill in these  languages it's absolutely meaningless to  make these kinds of comments based on  this one video rather the video is a  celebration of different languages that  she obviously enjoys and so you know if  something want to pursue absolute  perfection which I consider to be  elusive in a language that's fine if  other people want to have less than  perfection in a number of languages  that's equally fine  because whatever it is we set our own  goals in the language and the ultimate  sort of underlying goal always is  enjoyment and you know of all the people  that I have interacted with in English  who are not native speakers where we've  had a wonderful relationship friends or  business relationships and they're  speaking English less than perfectly  it's good we're communicating they're  enjoying the language they're enjoying  the ability to communicate in what is to  them a foreign language just as I enjoy  the ability to communicate in what is to  me a foreign language whether that be  Russian Chinese Japanese French Spanish  whatever and I'm well aware that I have  limitations in all of those languages  but they gave me a great sense of  enjoyment and so I think it's very  important you know as we come to the end  of the year we're gonna create maybe  some you know New Year's resolutions and  what we want to do it and if if language  learning is part of what we like to do  then I would say make sure your language  learning is grounded in your enjoyment  of the language or languages that you  are learning and don't criticize and  particularly don't correct other people  unless they ask you to do so and even  then I wouldn't do often and if people  are involved in teaching I think if you  can ignite the fire of interest and  enjoyment in in language learning and  forget all the testing of grammar  because all those things kick in only  very very slowly but if you can get  people motivated and they realize what a  rich world language learning brings them  that that would be job well done so I  wish everyone a Happy New Year enjoy  your life returning you learn to my  everyone enjoy the process I will see  you in the new year  bye for now
 

